  // eyeball is shaded in its own frame (EYE_FWD: x toward the ear, y up, z the gaze; the globe of radius 1): a clear cornea
  // (a sphere of 0.65 globe radii through the limbus, 7.8 of 12 mm, its apex 1.08 out) over an iris in the limbus plane,
  // seen through the cornea by refraction (aqueous humour n = 1.336), so the iris sits behind the cornea and shifts with the
  // view; the cornea is a sharp, wet mirror (f0 0.025, n = 1.376) of the key light and its softbox (eyeEnv) and of the room.
  // The iris has radial fibres, a collarette, crypts and a dark limbal ring, the pupil a crisp edge; the sclera is a warm
  // off-white with faint veins toward the corners; the lids (eyeLids()) cast a contact shadow, and a tear meniscus lies
  // along the lower lid. The detail fades out as the eye gets small on screen, so a full-body view does not sparkle.
